CRUD (Operations) :
-------------------

CRUD stands for Create, Read, Update, and Delete, representing the fundamental operations for
managing data in databases and APIs. These operations are mapped to HTTP methods like POST,
GET, PUT/PATCH, and DELETE, respectively.

Create (POST):
Adds new data or resources to the database or API. For example, posting a new blog entry.

Read (GET):
Retrieves existing data or resources. For example, viewing a blog post.

Update (PUT/PATCH):
Modifies existing data or resources.

PUT: Replaces the entire resource with the new data.
PATCH: Updates specific fields of a resource without replacing the entire resource. For example, updating a user profile.

Delete (DELETE):
Removes data or resources from the database or API. For example, deleting a blog post.